-- What the informal proofs of sag/zmt-descent open, declaration by
-- declaration (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6), for 129 central declarations.
-- Each list was compared with the file comment of its declaration.
-- Besides the notions each proof is about (mev, lower, pw, pow, mapM,
-- comb, lin, sum, app, cat, inj*, mapE, leaf, lift, res, mexpr, Holds,
-- In, Coords, blocks, mono, sN, chi, ...), the lists contain
--   * carriers: Fin, Hom, Preserves, Vec, Mat, Ex, Vn, Trunc.carrier/image
--     ('an element of the span is merely a combination');
--   * the quotient aliases of presented algebras and of A[X] (Carrier, Q,
--     image, include, addQ, mulQ, operation, Descend.choose/map, induction,
--     constant, inclusion, generators, algebra, ring): the CRing fields of
--     PresentedAlgebra.ring and Extension.ring are identified with the
--     quotient operations by unfolding these aliases, as in
--     sag/zmt-weighted4;
--   * 'by definition of the evaluation': ev (m+1) c = Given.extend, and
--     extend = backward = Evaluate.extension (CoefficientBase.Eval.ev-var,
--     CharacteristicMonic.Trick.annih), and phi = PresentationExistence.To.extend
--     (ResidualAlgebra.Algebra.To.phi-y);
--   * 'by definition of the tower': A_(m+1) = A_m[C] (tower, ring, S, set);
--   * in QuotientFibre: the quotient-ring aliases of R/I and E/IE
--     (Carrier, Q, Rel, include, Add/Multiply.operation, Descend.map) and
--     the components of ModuleFinite;
--   * in CertificateSubalgebra/CertificateLocalisation: the subring
--     aliases (Carrier, ring, incl, E) and the localisation aliases of
--     PowerLocalization/MonoidLocalization (ring, Carrier, include,
--     Add/Multiply.operation, Fraction, Powers, Quot.Q/image/Descend);
--   * in the regressions over Z/4Z and Z, the ring tables (add, mul, neg,
--     iota, iotaN, one, negPos) evaluated on closed elements.
